' 4+1 physical view - UML deployment diagram of production
' Version 1.1 - 2026-11-10
' For: whoever deploys, operates or supports the application.
' Documented decision: the site runs on Vercel, the API and the email worker in the same Render service, the database on Supabase (always through the pooler in session mode) and SMTP on Brevo; GitHub Actions applies the migrations as the schema owner and launches the deploys (ADR 0009).
' Only what exists in production since 2026-11-09. Development (docker compose) is in c4/04-deployment-dev.puml.
' Same nodes and names as c4/04-deployment-prod.puml.
' Not drawn: what was not adopted (Caddy, virtual machine, GHCR, custom domain, daily backups; see ADR 0009), the secrets and the environment variables (docs/deployment/environment-variables.md).
@startuml physical
!include ../style.puml

title Physical view - production (T06)
left to right direction

node "User's browser" as C_BROWSER

node "Vercel (Hobby)" as PL_VERCEL {
    component "Vercel edge" as PL_VERCEL_EDGE
    artifact "Next.js application" as C_WEB
}

node "Render (free plan, Frankfurt)" as PL_RENDER {
    component "Render edge" as PL_RENDER_EDGE
    node "Public web service (Docker)" as PL_RENDER_API {
        artifact "ASP.NET Core API" as C_API
        artifact "Email worker" as C_WORKER
    }
}

node "Supabase (Free)" as PL_SUPABASE {
    component "Connection pooler" as PL_SUPAPOOL
    database "Database" as C_DB
}

node "Brevo" as PL_BREVO_NODE {
    component "SMTP server" <<external>> as PL_BREVO
}

node "GitHub Actions" as X_GHA {
    artifact "deploy.yml" as PL_DEPLOY
    artifact "prod-data.yml" as PL_PRODDATA
    artifact "Migration bundle" as PL_MIGBUNDLE
}

C_BROWSER --> PL_VERCEL_EDGE : Opens pages and calls /api/*\n[HTTPS, cookies]
PL_VERCEL_EDGE --> C_WEB : Routes the pages
PL_VERCEL_EDGE --> PL_RENDER_EDGE : Rewrites /api/*\n[HTTPS, Internet]
C_WEB --> PL_RENDER_EDGE : Server Components read the API\n[HTTPS, API_INTERNAL_URL]
PL_RENDER_EDGE --> C_API : Forwards the request\n[HTTP, PORT]
C_API --> PL_SUPAPOOL : Reads and writes as sportsbooking_app\n[SQL, TLS]
C_WORKER --> PL_SUPAPOOL : Claims the outbox and saves the result\n[SQL, TLS]
PL_SUPAPOOL --> C_DB : Connects\n[PostgreSQL]
C_WORKER --> PL_BREVO : Sends the email\n[SMTP, StartTls]
PL_DEPLOY --> PL_MIGBUNDLE : Builds and runs
PL_PRODDATA --> PL_MIGBUNDLE : migrate-only
PL_MIGBUNDLE --> PL_SUPAPOOL : Applies the migrations as postgres\n[SQL, TLS]
PL_PRODDATA --> PL_SUPAPOOL : Runs the commands as postgres\n[SQL, TLS]
PL_DEPLOY --> PL_RENDER_API : Triggers the deploy of this commit\n[Deploy hook]
PL_DEPLOY --> PL_VERCEL : Publishes the build\n[Vercel CLI]
@enduml
